from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib,difflib,datetime
root=Path('physics');base=root/'research/physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2-owner-step5-qft-referrals'
subjects=['lem-qftx-wavefront-chart-invariance','thm-qftx-wavefront-product','thm-qftx-scalar-eg-induction']
changes={}
for id in subjects:
 p=root/'items'/f'{id}.md';t=p.read_text();changes[id]=[t,t,[]]
def replace(id,old,new,where):
 row=changes[id];assert row[1].count(old)==1,(id,where,row[1].count(old));row[1]=row[1].replace(old,new);row[2].append({'location':where,'old':old,'new':new})
for id in subjects[:2]:
 t=changes[id][1];first=t.split('## Statement\n\n',1)[1].split('\n',1)[0]
 replace(id,first,'Assume Countable Choice. '+first,'Statement opening')
 before='## Statement references\n\n';replace(id,before,before+'[[def-countable-choice]]\n\n','Statement references')
id=subjects[2]
old=r'[F3] [[lem-qftx-microcausal-star-product]]: $\star_W$ is defined coefficientwise on the stated microcausal polynomial class by finitely many Hadamard contractions; its kernel has $W-W^{\mathsf T}=iE$ with causal support.'
new=r'[F3] [[lem-qftx-microcausal-star-product]]: $\star_W$ is defined coefficientwise on the stated microcausal polynomial class by finitely many Hadamard contractions and preserves that class. Separately, [[def-qftx-local-time-ordered-system]] assumes $W-W^{\mathsf T}=iE$ for a fixed $E$ supported on causal pairs; this is a premise of the free datum, not a conclusion of the contraction lemma.'
replace(id,old,new,'Facts & Assumptions F3')
old=changes[id][1].split('\n6.1 ',1)[1].split('\n\n7.1 ',1)[0]
new=r'''6.1 Keep together all components that mix under Lorentz transformations. At fixed input field degrees and homogeneous derivative degrees, take the finite-dimensional space $L$ of balanced input-label tensors and the finite-dimensional space $O$ of remaining field-jet labels occurring in their finite graph expansion, enlarging each to contain its full Lorentz orbit. The substitution $p_a\mapsto\Lambda^{\mathsf T}p_a$ of [F11] defines their representations $R_L,R_O$; linear substitutions preserve field degree and homogeneous derivative degree, so these enlargements remain finite. In relative dimension $d=4(n-1)$ put $A_\Lambda(z_1,\ldots,z_{n-1})=(\Lambda z_1,\ldots,\Lambda z_{n-1})$ and $U_\Lambda=(A_{\Lambda^{-1}})^*\otimes R_O(\Lambda)$ on $\mathcal D'(\mathbb R^d)\otimes O$. Regard the chosen numerical coefficients collectively as $t^1\in\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb C}(L,\mathcal D'(\mathbb R^d)\otimes O)$, with combined action $(\Lambda\cdot t)(b)=U_\Lambda t(R_L(\Lambda)^{-1}b)$. These are representations by the pullback and substitution laws. On the punctured relative space the collective coefficient $t^0$ is fixed by this combined action: the free kernels are invariant, their differentiated components transform by the chain rule, and the already covariant lower-order products agree on the causal-cover overlaps. A fixed coordinate derivative component need not be scalar invariant. [F1, F11, step 3.1, step 4.1, step 5.1, construct, algebra]

6.2 For the finite block in step 6.1 choose a common finite engineering upper bound $B$ compatible with its homogeneous label degrees and the finitely many lower-order counterterms. Linear coordinate changes commute with positive dilations and preserve these bounds. Put $J_N=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb C}\{\partial^\alpha\delta_0:|\alpha|\le N\}$, where $N=\lfloor B-d\rfloor$ when $B\ge d$, and put $J_N=0$ when $B<d$. The permitted local corrections form the invariant subspace $V$ of $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb C}(L,J_N\otimes O)$ satisfying the labelwise engineering bounds and the linear identities of the balanced coefficients. This space is finite-dimensional. Lorentz substitutions preserve each homogeneous degree and delta-derivative order, while [F11] makes the derivative identities equivariant, proving invariance of this subspace. Differentiate the combined action to obtain $\rho(X)$ and put $c(X)=\rho(X)t^1$. Restriction commutes with the action, and step 6.1 gives $\rho(X)t^0=0$, so $c(X)$ is supported at the relative origin. It obeys the same engineering bounds and identities; [F8] and [F10] therefore place it in $V$. Smooth differentiation is justified by differentiating the transformed compact test densities in their fixed-support smooth topology; the finite-order distribution bound then permits pairing. The representation law gives $c([X,Y])=\rho(X)c(Y)-\rho(Y)c(X)$, so $c:\mathfrak{so}(1,3)\to V$ is exactly a real-linear cocycle in the finite-dimensional complex module required by [F9]. [F8, F9, F10, F11, step 6.1, algebra]

6.3 Apply [F9] to this module and cocycle to obtain $v\in V$ with $c(X)=\rho(X)v$. Thus $t^1-v$ has zero infinitesimal combined defect, retains the engineering bounds, and agrees with $t^0$ off the diagonal. Its combined orbit is constant along each one-parameter subgroup by the preceding smooth test-pairing argument. Along a smooth group path $g(s)$ the orbit derivative is the transported infinitesimal action of $g(s)^{-1}g'(s)$ and hence is zero. In the identity component every point is reachable by a piecewise smooth path: the set reachable from the identity and its complement are open, using straight paths in coordinate balls. Connectedness therefore gives full $SO^+(1,3)$ covariance. Work separately in homogeneous balanced-label degrees, whose finite spaces are Lorentz invariant, and recover total-derivative descendants by [F11]; the resulting corrections are compatible on their algebraic direct sum and preserve representation independence. The choices of these finite-block corrections are permitted by [A1]. Translation covariance is retained because every correction is a relative delta jet lifted by the same center-coordinate integral as in step 5.1. [A1, F1, F8, F9, F11, step 5.1, step 6.1, step 6.2, algebra]'''
new=new.replace('6.2 ', '7.1 ').replace('6.3 ', '8.1 ').replace('step 6.2', 'step 7.1')
replace(id,'6.1 '+old,new,'Proof old 6.1 replaced by 6.1, 7.1, 8.1')
replace(id,'\n7.1 Symmetrize','\n9.1 Symmetrize','old Proof 7.1 relabelled 9.1')
replace(id,'\n8.1 The construction','\n10.1 The construction','old Proof 8.1 relabelled 10.1')
replace(id,'[A1, F1, F3, step 1.1, step 7.1]','[A1, F1, F3, step 1.1, step 9.1]','final QED tag')
replace(id,'[A1, F1, F3, F8, F11, step 3.1, step 6.1, algebra]','[A1, F1, F3, F8, F11, step 3.1, step 8.1, algebra]','Proof 7.1 tag')
rows=[]
for id,(old,new,edits) in changes.items():
 before=base/'preimages'/f'{id}.md';after=base/'proposed'/f'{id}.md';patch=base/f'{id}.patch';before.write_text(old);after.write_text(new);patch.write_text(''.join(difflib.unified_diff(old.splitlines(True),new.splitlines(True),fromfile=f'a/items/{id}.md',tofile=f'b/items/{id}.md')))
 rows.append({'id':id,'source':f'items/{id}.md','preimage':str(before.relative_to(root)),'candidate':str(after.relative_to(root)),'patch':str(patch.relative_to(root)),'raw_before_sha256':hashlib.sha256(old.encode()).hexdigest(),'raw_candidate_sha256':hashlib.sha256(new.encode()).hexdigest(),'patch_sha256':hashlib.sha256(patch.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'public_interface_change':id!=subjects[2],'edits':edits})
(base/'proposal-index.json').write_text(json.dumps({'version':1,'run':'physics-non-fluid-129-2026-10-21-r2','scientific_owner':'/root/step5_qft_referrals','review_repair_cycle':1,'maximum_cycles':2,'status':'unapplied-proposals','native_acceptance':False,'source_write_authority':False,'proposals':rows},indent=2)+'\n')
